  "difficulty_reason": "A single assumed generator detects eventual cohomological boundedness of an arbitrary unbounded quasi-coherent derived object, without an ample line bundle or Noetherian hypothesis. The proof spreads eventual vanishing to all perfect probes via finite thick generation, then uses closed-support Koszul truncation detection and a lifted local generator in a finite-affine induction to force global boundedness. This compatibility of the derived boundedness structure with a global generator is stronger than mere nonzero-object detection.",
